  "worked_solution": "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}^{2} & \\ge 5x \\\\ -2{x}^{2}-5x & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=-2{x}^{2}-5x$ lies above the $x$-axis or touches this axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}^{2}-5x & =0 \\\\ -x(2x+5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-\\frac{5}{2}$ and $x=0,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/33b031b579d84d633e4dcc56c912333327449fcbc6969eeceb34e209c4d308d1.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n-2{x}^{2}-5x\\ge 0,\n$$\n\n we look for the part of the parabola that is above the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\n Based on the graph, the solution is $-\\frac{5}{2}\\le x\\le 0.$ \n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in [-\\frac{5}{2},0].$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
